; Declares (universe) because the corpus test reads two things dune cannot
; track: the committed golden specs under trading/test_data/, and
; dev/weekly-picks/live-config-overrides.sexp, which lives OUTSIDE the dune
; root (the root is trading/, and dev/ is its sibling). Without it, editing a
; golden or the live overrides would not invalidate the cached test result and
; the drift check would silently stop enforcing. Same reasoning as the
; (universe) branch taken by the devtools checks in
; trading/devtools/checks/dune.

(tests
 (names test_golden_live_drift)
 (modules test_golden_live_drift)
 (deps (universe))
 (libraries
  ounit2
  core
  core_unix.filename_unix
  matchers
  golden_live_drift_lib
  backtest
  weinstein_trading.strategy))
